IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lt-common`
IMPORT `lta-core`

-- Cases for lta-core.l4: the Land Tax Act 2000, the Land Tax Rating Act 2000 and the Land Tax Regulations 2021 (Tas).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited texts. The Schedule 1 and s 7 arithmetic was checked in an
-- independent calculator written from the statutory words (scratchpad au-tas-4/hand.py); no value was copied from the
-- encoding's output. Regulative rules: asserted with EVALTRACE where the trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an
-- "-- expect:" line where it ends in a breach or with an obligation still pending. Clock: days.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- Land Tax Act 2000 core`

§§ `The years covered`

#ASSERT `the deposited land tax provisions apply to` 2026
#ASSERT `the deposited land tax provisions apply to` 2030
#ASSERT NOT (`the deposited land tax provisions apply to` 2025)

§§ `Rating Act Schedule 1 and s 7`

-- Less than $125 000: nil. $125 000 exactly: $50 (a $50 step, finding 5).
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 124999 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 125000 EQUALS 50
-- $300 000: $50 + 0.45c x 175 000 = $50 + $787.50 = $837.50.
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 300000 EQUALS 837.50
-- $400 000: $50 + 0.45c x 275 000 = $1 287.50.
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 400000 EQUALS 1287.50
-- The two scales meet at $500 000: $50 + 0.45c x 375 000 = $1 737.50, the figure in item 3.
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 500000 EQUALS 1737.50
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 499999 EQUALS 1737.4955
-- $600 000: $1 737.50 + 1.5c x 100 000 = $3 237.50.
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 600000 EQUALS 3237.50
-- $1 000 000: $1 737.50 + 1.5c x 500 000 = $9 237.50.
#ASSERT `land tax under Schedule 1 on` 1000000 EQUALS 9237.50

-- s 7 rounding to a multiple of 10 cents (finding 6).
-- $125 011: $50.0495 = 5004.95 cents; 4.95 cents remain, 5 or less: down to $50.00.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 125011) EQUALS 50
-- $125 012: $50.054 = 5005.4 cents; 5.4 cents remain, more than 5: up to $50.10.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 125012) EQUALS 50.10
-- $125 100: $50.45; exactly 5 cents remain, "5 or less": down to $50.40.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 125100) EQUALS 50.40
-- $125 111: $50.4995; 9.95 cents remain: up to $50.50.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 125111) EQUALS 50.50
-- $300 001: $837.5045; 0.45 cents remain: down to $837.50.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 300001) EQUALS 837.50
-- $499 999: $1 737.4955; 9.55 cents remain: up to $1 737.50.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 499999) EQUALS 1737.50
-- An amount already a multiple of 10 cents is unchanged.
#ASSERT `rounded under s 7` 837.50 EQUALS 837.50

§§ `ss 3A, 3B and 11A -- owners and interests`

#ASSERT `is an owner under s 3A` `registered owner of the fee simple, with no life estate in another person`
#ASSERT `is an owner under s 3A` `registered as entitled to a life estate`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an owner under s 3A` `owner of the fee simple in remainder after another person's life estate`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an owner under s 3A` `no estate in the land`)

`sole holding` MEANS `Holding` WITH
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS 100
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS 1
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS 0

`one of two joint tenants` MEANS `Holding` WITH
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS 100
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS 2
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS 0

`one of three joint tenants` MEANS `Holding` WITH
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS 100
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS 3
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS 0

-- A couple holding 70% as joint tenants, Housing Australia 30% under Help to Buy.
`one of a Help to Buy couple` MEANS `Holding` WITH
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS 70
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS 2
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS 30

-- The same couple if s 11A did not apply: 35% each.
`one of the couple without s 11A` MEANS `Holding` WITH
    `share of the land held, in percent` IS 70
    `number of joint tenants of that share` IS 2
    `Help to Buy share of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, in percent` IS 0

#ASSERT `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `sole holding` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `one of two joint tenants` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `is an owner of at least a 50% interest` `one of two joint tenants`
-- s 3B: three joint tenants hold a third each, so none is an owner of at least a 50% interest (finding 3).
#ASSERT `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `one of three joint tenants` EQUALS 100 DIVIDED BY 3
#ASSERT NOT (`is an owner of at least a 50% interest` `one of three joint tenants`)
-- s 11A: 35 of the 70 counted = 50% (finding 4).
#ASSERT `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `one of a Help to Buy couple` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `is an owner of at least a 50% interest` `one of a Help to Buy couple`
#ASSERT `the interest in percent counted for land tax` `one of the couple without s 11A` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT NOT (`is an owner of at least a 50% interest` `one of the couple without s 11A`)

§§ `s 6 -- principal residence land`

`my own home` MEANS `Residence at 1 July` WITH
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS TRUE
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS FALSE
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS FALSE
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS FALSE

`my home after I move to a retirement village` MEANS `Residence at 1 July` WITH
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS TRUE
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS FALSE
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS FALSE

`my home where my former spouse lives` MEANS `Residence at 1 July` WITH
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS FALSE
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS FALSE
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS TRUE
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS FALSE

`my temporary home while my burnt home's classification is extended` MEANS `Residence at 1 July` WITH
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS TRUE
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS FALSE
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS FALSE
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS TRUE

`my shack` MEANS `Residence at 1 July` WITH
    `the principal residence of an owner of at least a 50% interest is on the land` IS FALSE
    `that owner occupies premises in a retirement village as their principal place of residence` IS FALSE
    `the principal residence of a related person of such an owner is on the land` IS FALSE
    `a s 37B extension is in force for other land of the owner` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `is principal residence land under s 6(1)` `my own home`
-- s 6(8): once in a retirement village, the owner's other land is not their principal place of residence.
#ASSERT NOT (`is principal residence land under s 6(1)` `my home after I move to a retirement village`)
-- s 3 "related person" (a): a former spouse.
#ASSERT `is principal residence land under s 6(1)` `my home where my former spouse lives`
-- s 37B(2): no other principal residence land during an extension.
#ASSERT NOT (`is principal residence land under s 6(1)` `my temporary home while my burnt home's classification is extended`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is principal residence land under s 6(1)` `my shack`)

`the garden block next door` MEANS `Adjoining land` WITH
    `adjoins the principal residence land` IS TRUE
    `is on a separate title held by the owner of the principal residence land` IS TRUE
    `has no dwelling used as a place of residence` IS TRUE
    `is used by that owner solely in conjunction with the principal residence land` IS TRUE
    `the owner receives no income from its use` IS TRUE
    `the owner of at least 50% of the principal residence land owns at least 50% of this land` IS TRUE

`the block next door, let for grazing` MEANS `Adjoining land` WITH
    `adjoins the principal residence land` IS TRUE
    `is on a separate title held by the owner of the principal residence land` IS TRUE
    `has no dwelling used as a place of residence` IS TRUE
    `is used by that owner solely in conjunction with the principal residence land` IS FALSE
    `the owner receives no income from its use` IS FALSE
    `the owner of at least 50% of the principal residence land owns at least 50% of this land` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `is principal residence land under s 6(2)` `the garden block next door`
#ASSERT NOT (`is principal residence land under s 6(2)` `the block next door, let for grazing`)

`Mum's home, the year after she died` MEANS `After a sole owner's death` WITH
    `the land was principal residence land under s 6(1) on the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the sole owner on that day died on or after it and before this 1 July` IS TRUE
    `that owner's principal residence was on the land on the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the land has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative` IS TRUE

`Mum's home, transferred to a beneficiary before 1 July` MEANS `After a sole owner's death` WITH
    `the land was principal residence land under s 6(1) on the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the sole owner on that day died on or after it and before this 1 July` IS TRUE
    `that owner's principal residence was on the land on the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the land has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative` IS FALSE

`Mum's garden block` MEANS `Adjoining land after a sole owner's death` WITH
    `was adjoining principal residence land under s 6(2) on the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `on this 1 July is on a separate title held by the owner, with no dwelling used as a residence, and owned at least 50% by the owner of at least 50% of the main land` IS TRUE
    `no income has been derived from it since the previous 1 July` IS TRUE
    `it has not since been sold or transferred, other than to the personal representative` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `continues as principal residence land under s 6(10)-(11)` `Mum's home, the year after she died`
#ASSERT NOT (`continues as principal residence land under s 6(10)-(11)` `Mum's home, transferred to a beneficiary before 1 July`)
#ASSERT `continues as principal residence land under s 6(12)` `Mum's home, the year after she died` `Mum's garden block`
#ASSERT NOT (`continues as principal residence land under s 6(12)` `Mum's home, transferred to a beneficiary before 1 July` `Mum's garden block`)

§§ `s 37B -- disasters`

`the bushfire` MEANS `Disaster` WITH
    `the land is classified as principal residence land or primary production land` IS TRUE
    `a flood, fire or other similar disaster made it unsuitable for that use` IS TRUE
    `the disaster was outside the owner's control` IS TRUE

`the fire I lit` MEANS `Disaster` WITH
    `the land is classified as principal residence land or primary production land` IS TRUE
    `a flood, fire or other similar disaster made it unsuitable for that use` IS TRUE
    `the disaster was outside the owner's control` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the classification may be extended under s 37B` `the bushfire`
#ASSERT NOT (`the classification may be extended under s 37B` `the fire I lit`)
#ASSERT `the longest s 37B extension, in years` EQUALS 2

§§ `ss 7 and 8 -- classes`

`the sheep farm` MEANS `Primary production` WITH
    `an activity listed in s 7(2) is carried on on the land` IS TRUE
    `it is carried on in a business-like manner with a reasonable expectation of profit` IS TRUE
    `the land is used substantially for it` IS TRUE
    `the land is a private timber reserve, permanent timber production zone land or under a certified forest practices plan` IS FALSE

`the hobby farm` MEANS `Primary production` WITH
    `an activity listed in s 7(2) is carried on on the land` IS TRUE
    `it is carried on in a business-like manner with a reasonable expectation of profit` IS FALSE
    `the land is used substantially for it` IS TRUE
    `the land is a private timber reserve, permanent timber production zone land or under a certified forest practices plan` IS FALSE

`the private timber reserve` MEANS `Primary production` WITH
    `an activity listed in s 7(2) is carried on on the land` IS FALSE
    `it is carried on in a business-like manner with a reasonable expectation of profit` IS FALSE
    `the land is used substantially for it` IS FALSE
    `the land is a private timber reserve, permanent timber production zone land or under a certified forest practices plan` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `is primary production land under s 7` `the sheep farm`
#ASSERT NOT (`is primary production land under s 7` `the hobby farm`)
#ASSERT `is primary production land under s 7` `the private timber reserve`

#ASSERT `the class of land that is` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `principal residence land`
#ASSERT `the class of land that is` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `primary production land`
#ASSERT `the class of land that is` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `general land`
-- Both: reported as principal residence land (finding 9).
#ASSERT `the class of land that is` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `principal residence land`

§§ `s 19(a)-(b) and reg 5 -- the pensioner exemption`

`a pensioner owning half` MEANS `Pensioner owner` WITH
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS TRUE
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS FALSE
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS FALSE
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS FALSE

`a pensioner owning a third` MEANS `Pensioner owner` WITH
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS TRUE
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS FALSE
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS FALSE
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS FALSE

`a war widow with the gold card` MEANS `Pensioner owner` WITH
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS FALSE
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS TRUE
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS FALSE
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS FALSE

`a TPI veteran` MEANS `Pensioner owner` WITH
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS FALSE
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS FALSE
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS TRUE
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS TRUE

`a special rate pensioner not found TPI` MEANS `Pensioner owner` WITH
    `owns 50% or more of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a current Pensioner Concession Card` IS FALSE
    `holds a Repatriation Health Card -- For All Conditions with a war widow or war widower endorsement` IS FALSE
    `receives a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS TRUE
    `is totally and permanently incapacitated` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `principal residence land` `a pensioner owning half`
#ASSERT `is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `primary production land` `a pensioner owning half`
#ASSERT NOT (`is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `general land` `a pensioner owning half`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `principal residence land` `a pensioner owning a third`)
#ASSERT `is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `principal residence land` `a war widow with the gold card`
#ASSERT `is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `principal residence land` `a TPI veteran`
#ASSERT NOT (`is exempt land under s 19(a) or (b)` `principal residence land` `a special rate pensioner not found TPI`)

§§ `ss 3 and 26 -- home businesses and apportionment`

`the hairdresser in the front room` MEANS `Home business` WITH
    `is operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located` IS TRUE
    `is operated from that dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not solely commercial` IS TRUE
    `is operated by the owner, or the owner's spouse, sibling, child or parent` IS TRUE
    `the land is that person's sole permanent business premises` IS TRUE
    `percentage of the dwelling's floor area ordinarily used for it` IS 50

`the hairdresser using most of the house` MEANS `Home business` WITH
    `is operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located` IS TRUE
    `is operated from that dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not solely commercial` IS TRUE
    `is operated by the owner, or the owner's spouse, sibling, child or parent` IS TRUE
    `the land is that person's sole permanent business premises` IS TRUE
    `percentage of the dwelling's floor area ordinarily used for it` IS 51

`the business run by a tenant` MEANS `Home business` WITH
    `is operated from land on which a prescribed dwelling is located` IS TRUE
    `is operated from that dwelling or a building ordinarily found on residential land that is not solely commercial` IS TRUE
    `is operated by the owner, or the owner's spouse, sibling, child or parent` IS FALSE
    `the land is that person's sole permanent business premises` IS TRUE
    `percentage of the dwelling's floor area ordinarily used for it` IS 20

#ASSERT `is a qualifying home business` `the hairdresser in the front room`
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying home business` `the hairdresser using most of the house`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying home business` `the business run by a tenant`)

-- A 600 m2 block, a 100 m2 upper floor (the ground floor not counted), a 70 m2 shop: land area 700 m2 (s 26(2A)),
-- principal residence proportion 630/700 = 0.9.
`the house with a shop` MEANS `Land area` WITH
    `area of the land` IS 600
    `area of all additional floors above or below ground level, not the ground floor, of all structures` IS 100
    `part of that land area used for purposes other than the principal residence` IS 70

`the house with no other use` MEANS `Land area` WITH
    `area of the land` IS 600
    `area of all additional floors above or below ground level, not the ground floor, of all structures` IS 100
    `part of that land area used for purposes other than the principal residence` IS 0

#ASSERT `the land area under s 26(2A)` `the house with a shop` EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `the proportion of land area used as the principal residence` `the house with a shop` EQUALS 0.9
#ASSERT `the land value is apportioned under s 26` `the house with a shop` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the land value is apportioned under s 26` `the house with a shop` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the land value is apportioned under s 26` `the house with a shop` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the land value is apportioned under s 26` `the house with no other use` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the principal residence proportion under s 26` `the house with a shop` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0.9
#ASSERT `the principal residence proportion under s 26` `the house with a shop` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the principal residence proportion under s 26` `the house with no other use` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1

