-- A purchase completed on 1 July takes effect after the commencement of the year (finding 10).
#ASSERT NOT (`was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `bought, completed 1 July 2026` 2026)
#ASSERT `was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `bought, completed 1 July 2026` 2027
#ASSERT `was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `sold, completed 1 July 2026` 2026
#ASSERT NOT (`was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `sold, completed 30 June 2026` 2026)
#ASSERT `was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `sold, completed 30 June 2026` 2025
#ASSERT NOT (`was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `the remainderman` 2026)
#ASSERT `was the owner at the commencement of the financial year` `the life tenant` 2026

-- s 10(2): due on the Commissioner's date, or on completion of a sale if earlier.
#ASSERT `the day land tax is due under s 10(2)` (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 20
#ASSERT `the day land tax is due under s 10(2)` (YMD 2026 9 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 15
#ASSERT `the day land tax is due under s 10(2)` (YMD 2026 9 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 8 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 15

-- s 13(1): "exceeds $500". $225 000 of general land gives exactly $500: no instalments; $225 012 gives $500.054, rounded
-- under s 7 to $500.10: instalments may be accepted; $225 011 gives $500.0495, rounded to $500.00: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commissioner may accept instalments under s 13(1)` (`rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 225000)))
#ASSERT `the Commissioner may accept instalments under s 13(1)` (`rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 225012))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commissioner may accept instalments under s 13(1)` (`rounded under s 7` (`land tax under Schedule 1 on` 225011)))

#ASSERT `each joint owner is liable for the full tax under s 14(2)(b)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`each joint owner is liable for the full tax under s 14(2)(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `READING: land owned jointly is assessed apart from land a joint owner owns alone`

§§ `ss 37 and 37A -- rebates`

`built and moved in during the year` MEANS `Building a home` WITH
    `the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year` IS TRUE
    `during the year a dwelling was built on the land and occupied as principal residence by an owner of at least 50% or a related person` IS TRUE
    `during the year the occupier owned other principal residence land in Tasmania, or a principal residence elsewhere in Australia` IS FALSE

-- Moving from a home the builder still owned at 1 July fails s 37(1)(c) (finding 13).
`built and moved from my old home, sold in the same year` MEANS `Building a home` WITH
    `the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year` IS TRUE
    `during the year a dwelling was built on the land and occupied as principal residence by an owner of at least 50% or a related person` IS TRUE
    `during the year the occupier owned other principal residence land in Tasmania, or a principal residence elsewhere in Australia` IS TRUE

`bought the block after 1 July` MEANS `Building a home` WITH
    `the owner was an owner at the start of the financial year` IS FALSE
    `during the year a dwelling was built on the land and occupied as principal residence by an owner of at least 50% or a related person` IS TRUE
    `during the year the occupier owned other principal residence land in Tasmania, or a principal residence elsewhere in Australia` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `may apply for a rebate under s 37` `built and moved in during the year`
#ASSERT NOT (`may apply for a rebate under s 37` `built and moved from my old home, sold in the same year`)
#ASSERT NOT (`may apply for a rebate under s 37` `bought the block after 1 July`)

-- Bought the new home on 15 May 2026, still owned and lived in the old home on 1 July 2026; contracted to sell the old
-- home on 10 September 2026; the buyer took possession on 20 October 2026; no rent.
`the move in 2026` MEANS `Moving between two homes` WITH
    `the financial year` IS 2026
    `at 1 July the owner owned 50% or more of principal residence land and 50% or more of other land` IS TRUE
    `the other land was bought to become the owner's principal residence land, or was it in the 3 months before 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the day the owner became owner of the principal residence land` IS YMD 2012 2 1
    `the day the owner became owner of the other land` IS YMD 2026 5 15
    `the principal residence land was the owner's principal residence land in the 3 months before 1 July` IS TRUE
    `the other land became the owner's principal residence land during the financial year` IS TRUE
    `the day the owner contracted to sell or otherwise disposed of one of the two` IS YMD 2026 9 10
    `the new owner took possession during the financial year` IS TRUE
    `rent or other income was derived from either while the owner owned both` IS FALSE
    `the owner recovered a proportion of the land tax from the buyer under s 40(1)` IS FALSE

-- The new home bought on 15 March 2026, more than 3 months before 1 July (s 37A(3)(a)).
`the move with the new home bought in March` MEANS `Moving between two homes` WITH
